WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.066 --> 00:00:07.527
Pluck woke up one morning earlier than usual.

2
00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:12.589
He could hear his friends outside singing, "Get up!

3
00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:13.589
Get up!

4
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.530
It's a new day!"

5
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.631
"What should I do today?"

6
00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:19.652
he wondered.

7
00:00:19.672 --> 00:00:25.955
"I could pick worms, glide through the air, or clean my feathers.

8
00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:29.136
But none of that sounds like fun."

9
00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:31.993
Pluck was not very excited about the new day.

10
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:36.574
So Pluck flew off to the riverbank to visit his friend, Duckie.

11
00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:38.735
"Hi Duckie!"

12
00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:41.455
Pluck called as he swooped down to the bank.

13
00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.956
"Well hello, Pluck.

14
00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:46.897
What a nice surprise to see you!"

15
00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:48.337
said Duckie.

16
00:00:48.357 --> 00:00:51.658
"Do you have any exciting plans for today?"

17
00:00:52.038 --> 00:00:52.558
said Pluck.

18
00:00:52.578 --> 00:00:55.639
"I am bored and don't know what to do."

19
00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:59.497
"Hmm." Duckie had to think hard.

20
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:05.799
"You could fly with me up and down the river, or we could dig in the mud to

21
00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:08.440
cool off our feet," he offered.

22
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.861
"No, thanks," said Pluck.

23
00:01:10.881 --> 00:01:15.383
"Well, if we have nothing to do at least we can be bored together."

24
00:01:16.623 --> 00:01:18.884
So Pluck and Duckie settled into the bank.

25
00:01:20.505 --> 00:01:23.266
They watched the flowers opening their faces to the sun.

26
00:01:24.347 --> 00:01:27.708
The flowers bent their stems to get as close to the light as possible.

27
00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:34.840
"Ooh!" They watched the fish jump at the bugs, trying to catch some lunch.

28
00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:40.144
The fish jumped high out of the water and made a lot of ripples when they fell back

29
00:01:40.244 --> 00:01:44.687
in. One fish splashed so much that he got Pluck and Duckie wet!

30
00:01:44.707 --> 00:01:53.493
"Hey!" While Pluck and Duckie were trying to shake off the water, they heard a little voice below

31
00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:54.734
them start to complain.

32
00:01:54.754 --> 00:01:57.256
"Please stop!

33
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.442
You are soaking my home!"

34
00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:05.667
They looked at the ground and saw a row of ants marching food into their hole.

35
00:02:07.248 --> 00:02:10.951
Sure enough, the water from their wings was getting the ground wet.

36
00:02:10.971 --> 00:02:13.693
"Oops! We're sorry!"

37
00:02:14.554 --> 00:02:16.896
Duckie said, and they moved to the side.

38
00:02:16.916 --> 00:02:20.179
"Those ants are really strong!"

39
00:02:20.759 --> 00:02:22.761
said Pluck, sounding very impressed.

40
00:02:23.481 --> 00:02:26.444
"Their food is five times bigger than they are!"

41
00:02:28.016 --> 00:02:31.058
After the ants left, Pluck and Duckie looked around.

42
00:02:32.579 --> 00:02:33.860
There was nothing left to see.

43
00:02:35.181 --> 00:02:37.283
Duckie lay down and stared at the sky.

44
00:02:37.303 --> 00:02:41.626
"That cloud looks like Big Farmer Parton!"

45
00:02:42.206 --> 00:02:44.828
said Duckie, sounding very sure of himself.

46
00:02:44.848 --> 00:02:47.830
"Yeah, I see him!

47
00:02:48.451 --> 00:02:51.313
And next to him is Dolly, his little girl!"

48
00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:52.573
said Pluck.

49
00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:58.558
As they lay there finding shapes in the clouds, the clouds began to turn pink and purple.

50
00:02:59.698 --> 00:03:04.982
This made the pictures in the sky even more beautiful and helped their imaginations find new shapes in

51
00:03:05.002 --> 00:03:05.522
the clouds.

52
00:03:07.284 --> 00:03:11.086
Eventually the pinkish purple colors began to turn to dark blue.

53
00:03:12.307 --> 00:03:16.130
While Pluck and Duckie were watching the clouds, the sun had begun to set.

54
00:03:17.571 --> 00:03:19.452
The flowers began to close their petals.

55
00:03:20.473 --> 00:03:21.593
The fish stopped jumping.

56
00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:25.276
The ants shut the door to their hole for the night.

57
00:03:26.476 --> 00:03:29.197
Pluck and Duckie could no longer see the cloud shapes.

58
00:03:30.258 --> 00:03:31.959
Pluck stood up and looked at Duckie.

59
00:03:31.979 --> 00:03:34.740
"Oh no!

60
00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.101
Duckie, we've wasted the whole day!

61
00:03:38.782 --> 00:03:41.263
We didn't do anything important!"

62
00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:42.964
he said disappointedly.

63
00:03:42.984 --> 00:03:45.565
"We didn't waste the day.

64
00:03:46.085 --> 00:03:47.206
We did nothing!"

65
00:03:47.846 --> 00:03:48.446
said Duckie.

66
00:03:48.466 --> 00:03:52.368
"What?" asked Pluck, sounding confused.

67
00:03:53.452 --> 00:03:57.253
"We don't have to be busy working to have an important day.

68
00:03:58.113 --> 00:04:03.955
Watching everyone else go about their day helped us appreciate the world around us.

69
00:04:04.895 --> 00:04:10.857
I had a wonderful time, but I won't be able to do it again for a little while."

70
00:04:10.877 --> 00:04:12.918
"Why not?"

71
00:04:13.598 --> 00:04:14.178
asked Pluck.

72
00:04:14.998 --> 00:04:17.979
He was starting to like the idea of doing nothing every day.

73
00:04:17.999 --> 00:04:21.480
"Because I have work to do tomorrow.

74
00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.329
Would you like to help?"

75
00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:26.031
"Sure," Pluck agreed.

76
00:04:26.051 --> 00:04:30.755
"Goodnight, Duckie," he said, as he watched him waddle home.

77
00:04:30.775 --> 00:04:38.061
"See you tomorrow for a brand new adventure," Duckie called back.

78
00:04:39.342 --> 00:04:41.464
Pluck flew home for a good night's sleep.
